Cell["\<\
Call init and symham first. hoppingData reads the solved real-space shell \
cache directly; it never reconstructs hopping amplitudes by Fourier-inverting \
H(k).\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"388d81d6-9fc5-46f1-8f03-a183887b3037"],

Cell["\<\
The returned Association uses H(R)[a,b]=<0,a|H|R,b> and H(k)=Sum_R H(R) Exp[2 \
Pi I k.R]. Lattice and WannierCenters are included when the current model \
supplies them.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a4f4f180-82f7-480b-8394-84a7b032a2b4"],

Cell["\<\
hoppingData returns $Failed and issues a message when the shell selection is \
invalid or unprepared, parameter values remain symbolic, the requested symham \
option combination was not cached, or cached real-space data are \
inconsistent. It does not repair the input or switch to an approximate \
fallback.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b789a889-323a-4c79-a125-86a05b765bbe"],

